<tr><td colspan=2><font face='Tahoma,Arial,Helvetica' size=2>- Heads up.  If you're on the sniper deck, and conc jumping medics are killing you, you're not paying attention/are zoomed in too much of the time.

- EMP's -- they are exactly like they should be.  If you're one of those scouts that grabs all the ammo packs and runs out the door, the EMP is easily going to take you out (well, these scouts usually just end up dropping free ammo on the bridge when they get killed), same for any other class if you don't discard.  The EMP as it is encourages players to actually DISCARD and perhaps even help their teammates.

- as far as 4 MIRV's, perhaps this is good in theory, but in practice, you just get demomen coming to your ramp room, and you hear, prime, throw, prime, throw, prime, throw, prime, throw.  In TFC, the MIRV is way too powerful as compared to TF 1 -- in TF 1, it was reasonable to have 4, but in TFC, because of the damage it does, it is not.


---

Engineer tactic: in 2fort, put a dispenser on the spiral ramps, just around a corner.  Drop ammo right in front of it.  When a soldier comes down, he'll grab the ammo right as he's walloped by your detonating dispenser (you do have a key bound to detdispenser, right?).  Chances are he forgets that he picked up extra ammo, and forgets to discard.  If he survives, he's EMP bait when he gets to the bottom.
